# Project open questions — the *known unknowns*.
#
# An open question records something the project hasn't pinned an
# answer for. Three statuses shape its lifecycle:
#
#   open               — no committed answer. Codegen for any module
#                        whose requirements appear in this question's
#                        `affects[]` list is BLOCKED. Three exits:
#                        (a) a decision answers the question,
#                        (b) a decision commits a working default
#                            (status flips to `default_committed`),
#                        (c) a decision closes the question as moot.
#                        No CLI flag bypasses the gate — this is
#                        intentional friction so "decide later"
#                        leaves an audit trail.
#
#   default_committed  — a decision (`default_via`) commits a working
#                        assumption. `verify` carries a one-line
#                        falsification plan ("here's how I'll know
#                        my placeholder was wrong"). Codegen proceeds;
#                        the placeholder + verify text are inlined
#                        into the prompt walk for affected modules.
#
#   closed             — a decision (`closed_by`) resolved the
#                        question. The decision becomes the source of
#                        truth; the OQ entry persists as audit trail.
#
# `affects = [...]` lists the requirement ids the question affects.
# At least one entry is required — an open question that affects
# nothing should be rephrased into a decision or deleted.
#
# Delete the EXAMPLE entries below once the project has real OQs.

# EXAMPLE: an open question (codegen blocks until resolved).
